  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q13",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Is it possible for a regular polygon to have interior angles of size $132^{\\circ}$?\nExplain why or why not.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. $n=7.5$, but the number of sides must be a whole number.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}n&=\\frac{360}{180-I}\\\\n&=\\frac{360}{180-132}\\\\n&=\\frac{360}{48}\\\\n&=7.5\\end{align*}$$\nNo. A polygon must have a whole number of sides.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
